<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Biharea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Biharea (Hungarian: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>) is a village in Bihor County, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, near Oradea, the site of an early medieval earthwork fortress. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta Hungarorum</a> names it as the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menumorut">Menumorut</a>, a ruler said to have resisted the Hungarians around 900, and it later gave its name to the Hungarian county of Bihar. Excavations there have found remains from the 9th to 11th centuries.</p></div>
